WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:05.360
Superhero movies have been a major part of
the cinematic landscape of 2017, with Logan,

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.970
Wonder Woman, and Thor: Ragnarok standing
out from the crowd.

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:12.400
In 2018, it looks like the superhero genre
will dominate even more, kicking off in February

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:15.279
with a slate of movies that will keep fans
excited all year.

00:00:15.279 --> 00:00:19.180
Whether you prefer the Avengers, Spider-Man,
the X-Men, the Justice League, or even Pixar,

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:22.140
there will be at least one superhero movie
for you next year.

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:27.330
Here are the movies coming out in 2018 that
should excite any comic book fan.

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:28.640
Black Panther

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:32.480
Chadwick Boseman first debuted as the Black
Panther in Captain America: Civil War, but

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:35.780
his first solo outing should give us a much
more satisfying trip to Wakanda.

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:39.760
Directed by Ryan Coogler, the film clearly
follows the pattern of Guardians of the Galaxy

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:44.179
and Thor: Ragnarok in allowing a visionary
director to put his own spin on a Marvel movie

00:00:44.179 --> 00:00:46.210
rather than adhering to a house style.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:50.100
Black Panther's combination of high-octane
action and visual splendor is like nothing

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.789
else we've seen on screen before.

00:00:51.789 --> 00:00:55.639
Coogler is responsible for Fruitvale Station
and Creed, both of which starred Michael B.

00:00:55.639 --> 00:00:59.499
Jordan, and he'll re-team with his frequent
screen star in this movie as well, with Jordan

00:00:59.499 --> 00:01:01.359
playing villain Erik Killmonger.

00:01:01.359 --> 00:01:05.070
The rest of the impressive cast includes veterans
Angela Bassett and Forest Whitaker, alongside

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:09.600
popular up-and-comers Danai Gurira, Lupita
N'yongo and Daniel Kaluuya.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:12.930
From everything we've seen of Black Panther
so far, we're in for a wild ride with his

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:15.830
pic hits theaters on February 16th.

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:16.850
The New Mutants

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:21.220
This X-Men spinoff looks to play up its horror
aspects rather than resembling just another

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:22.950
ordinary superhero movie.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:27.090
The original 1980s New Mutants comic series
has always had one foot in the horror genre,

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:30.640
and this cinematic adaptation looks to capitalize
on that thrill appeal.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:33.300
The characters at the center are each marked
by dark roots.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:36.070
Magik is a demonic witch who literally grew
up in Hell.

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:37.640
Wolfsbane is a werewolf.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:40.820
Mirage is haunted by a demonic bear spirit
that wiped out her family.

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:44.280
From the trailer, it looks like the movie
is going to incorporate all of that and place

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:47.050
the characters in an unsettling institutional
setting.

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:51.080
The X-Men franchise has had its ups and downs,
but by far the best of its films has been

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:53.930
Logan, which had a much darker take than most.

00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:57.250
Superhero horror tales aren't your ordinary
popcorn fare, but who knows?

00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:01.200
Maybe The New Mutants will usher in a new
era altogether when it begins haunting the

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.270
cineplex on April 13th.

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:05.630
Avengers: Infinity War

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:10.640
No doubt, this is the event movie every Marvel
fan has been waiting for since the MCU first

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:12.780
launched with Iron Man a decade before.

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:16.670
The Avengers, the Guardians of the Galaxy,
Spider-Man, Doctor Strange, and more will

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:20.940
join forces to take on the ultimate threat
to the universe in Avengers: Infinity War.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:24.310
Thanos, who first appeared in the mid-credits
scene of The Avengers, has been working in

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:28.490
the background in the five years since, gathering
the Infinity Stones that will give him ultimate

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:30.130
power over space and time.

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:34.840
Now all of the heroes must unite to stop him
from ruling the universe—or destroying it.

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:38.370
This is going to be an epic like no superhero
movie before has been before, so count on

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:42.350
hearing a lot about that Infinity Gauntlet
when this thing blasts into theaters on May

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:43.670
4th.

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:45.090
Deadpool 2

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:48.980
Although Ryan Reynolds was previously picked
on for his first performance as the Merc with

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:52.850
a Mouth in X-Men: Origins - Wolverine, he
was able to redeem himself as the character

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:54.350
in 2016's Deadpool.

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:58.150
The film became both the highest grossing
X-Men movie and the highest grossing R-rated

00:02:58.150 --> 00:02:59.150
movie.

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:02.520
It's that R rating that enabled the film to
capture Wade Wilson's unique combination of

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:06.110
irreverent humor and extreme violence that
made his comics so popular.

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:08.319
"This is a different kinda superhero story."

00:03:08.319 --> 00:03:12.100
If he's able to recapture that tone again
in Deadpool 2, which features the first movie

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:15.990
appearances of Cable and Domino, the sequel
should bring even more four-letter words to

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:19.440
the big screen when it bows into theaters
June 1st.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:21.220
The Incredibles 2

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:25.030
More than a decade has passed since Pixar's
The Incredibles proved that not all superheroes

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:27.420
and villains have to originate in comic books.

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:32.050
The animated flick captured the tone and visual
style of classic superhero comics and blended

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:35.890
it with a wholesome family comedy about finding
the value in being different.

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:40.330
Given its success, an immediate sequel seemed
in order, but it's taken 14 years for Pixar

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:42.970
to finally put The Incredibles 2 on the release
slate.

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:46.100
The good news for fans of the original is
that we don't have to worry about the characters

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:50.390
having aged in the off-time, which means,
yes, Jack-Jack is still a baby who's making

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:52.800
a big old mess for those powerful parents.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:54.240
Check it out on June 15th.

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:01.900
Ant-Man and the Wasp

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:07.041
2015's Ant-Man turned out to be a fun and
successful superhero outing, but Ant-Man and

00:04:07.041 --> 00:04:10.959
the Wasp looks to increase the intrigue by
bringing in a second superhero in Evangeline

00:04:10.959 --> 00:04:12.720
Lilly's character Hope van Dyne.

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:16.209
She'll be the first Marvel heroine to have
her name in the title of a film, and even

00:04:16.209 --> 00:04:19.940
though Lilly is playing the original Wasp's
daughter, it's still exciting to see any version

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:23.180
of the Wasp join the Marvel Cinematic Universe
at long last.

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:28.060
Count on this one to be fun and refreshing
when it flies onto screens July 6th.

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:29.060
Venom

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:33.690
Not many details have emerged about this adaptation
of the popular Spider-Man villain, and occasional

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:34.720
anti-hero, Venom.

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:38.530
However, we know that Tom Hardy is playing
the title part and director Ruben Fleischer

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:39.530
will helm the pic.

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:43.900
Fleischer first proved he could effectively
mix humor and violence in 2009's Zombieland,

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:47.840
so if that's the direction this film takes,
it could be the Deadpool of the Sony Spider-Man

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:48.840
universe.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:52.190
It's hard to imagine how you can introduce
Venom in a film that doesn't include Spider-Man,

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:55.960
but hopefully they can divert attention from
that problem with a deft script and plenty

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:56.960
of action.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:00.810
We'll find out soon enough, as Venom arrives
in theaters October 5th.

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:02.570
X-Men: Dark Phoenix

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:07.320
After all the time travel and continuity chaos
of the last few X-Men movies, the ending of

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:11.850
X-Men: Apocalypse finally introduced a stable
team of heroes who can move forward as a unit.

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:14.889
Dark Phoenix will pick up with that collection
of heroes, but will immediately make them

00:05:14.889 --> 00:05:18.730
face Earth-shattering chaos as Jean Grey's
powers start spinning out of control.

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:22.700
There are also rumors that Dark Phoenix will
take the X-Men into outer space, a setting

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:25.750
for many of their comics stories not yet visited
in the movies.

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:30.510
If so, circle November 2nd, 2018, on your
calendar twice because this one will be a

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:31.889
must-see.

00:05:31.889 --> 00:05:33.949
Untitled Animated Spider-Man Movie

00:05:33.949 --> 00:05:38.190
When news was coming out about Spider-Man's
arrival in the MCU, a lot of fans were disappointed

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:42.120
that it was Peter Parker appearing in Spider-Man:
Homecoming rather than his successor in the

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:43.350
role, Miles Morales.

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:47.699
So, Sony has made an effort to appease those
fans by making an animated Spider-Man movie

00:05:47.699 --> 00:05:49.100
focused on Morales.

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:52.990
The character will be voiced by Shameik Moore,
and while not many other details are out so

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:56.540
far, this movie is already sounding like it
will be a lot of fun when it casts its web

00:05:56.540 --> 00:06:01.430
on audiences starting December 14th, 2018.

00:06:01.430 --> 00:06:02.430
Aquaman

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:05.350
Although Justice League certainly had its
share of flaws, one of the more appealing

00:06:05.350 --> 00:06:07.800
characters in the film was Jason Momoa's Aquaman.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:11.290
And in just over a year he'll get his own
movie to swim around in.

00:06:11.290 --> 00:06:15.330
In it, Amber Heard will return as Mera who
had a brief cameo in Justice League.

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:20.040
Patrick Wilson will play Aquaman's evil half-brother
the Ocean Master, while Yahya Abdul-Mateen

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:22.190
is set to appear as co-villain Black Manta.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:26.960
Meanwhile, Willem Dafoe plays the wise Atlantean
Vulko, with Nicole Kidman and Temuera Morrison

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:27.960
as Aquaman's parents.

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:31.669
On top of all that, the movie's directed by
James Wan, who's proven his merit with both

00:06:31.669 --> 00:06:33.250
thriller and action movies.

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:37.600
So, count on Aquaman to make a splash when
it lands in theaters December 21st.

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:38.560
"My man!"

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:42.500
Batman Ninja

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:46.620
Batman's seen and done a lot of things over
his decades as one of DC's premier crimefighters,

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:50.660
but he's never undertaken a quest quite like
the one he'll face in Batman Ninja.

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:54.580
This animated feature sees the Caped Crusader—along
with the Bat Family and some members of his

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:58.930
rogues' gallery—hurled through space and
time to medieval Japan, where they find themselves

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:01.030
in the midst of a battle between good and
evil.

00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:04.949
The animated project promises a fresh—and
visually stunning—perspective on some of

00:07:04.949 --> 00:07:09.000
the publisher's most venerable characters;
so, look for it on Blu-ray and DVD sometime

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.580
in 2018.

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:12.750
Suicide Squad: Hell to Pay

00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:17.050
The live-action Suicide Squad movie was something
less than a home run for Warner Bros. and

00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:21.199
DC, but the anti-hero group has been one of
the publisher's best-loved creations for years,

00:07:21.199 --> 00:07:24.759
and with the right adaptation, they could
easily make a more successful jump to the

00:07:24.759 --> 00:07:25.759
screen.

00:07:25.759 --> 00:07:28.509
Maybe animation is the answer—and we'll
find out in 2018, when Suicide Squad: Hell

00:07:28.509 --> 00:07:29.500
to Pay arrives.

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:38.680
Little is known about this outing at present,
but we do know that it will bring the Squad

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:43.840
into DC's Animated Movies continuity, marking
their first foray into the animated universe

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:46.889
that also contains the Justice League and
the Teen Titans.

00:07:46.889 --> 00:07:48.139
Thanks for watching!

00:07:48.139 --> 00:07:50.509
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:50.509 --> 00:07:52.820
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

